 Dear Catholic Heritage Centre Team,

I run *Lesser Known Singapore* (pikaia.github.io / YouTube
<https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore>), a non-commercial,
educational project dedicated to documenting overlooked history, local
heritage, and historical sites in Singapore.

I am writing to request permission to reproduce images from your website,
specifically from the page *The Parish Schools* (
https://history.catholic.sg/the-parish-schools/) for a post recounting my
early childhood memories at Montfort School.

Additionally, as my blog frequently covers Singaporean historical events
and as the Catholic Church played a significant role in Singapore=E2=80=99s
development, I may wish to reference or cite other pages on your site in
future posts. To ensure I comply with your copyright and usage guidelines
without troubling your team for every individual instance, could you please
share your general terms for non-commercial reproduction? Specifically, I
would appreciate details on:

   -

   Standard credit line or attribution requirements
   -

   Image resolution or watermarking conditions
   -

   Any applicable non-commercial licensing guidelines or fees

Thank you very much for your time, assistance, and work in preserving
Singapore=E2=80=99s heritage.

Warm regards,

Chris Lee chriskslee@gmail.com

pikaia.github.io

youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore
<https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore>

